164
00:10:37,710 --> 00:10:42,131
While the baby is in embryonic development,

165
00:10:42,548 --> 00:10:45,759
during the first trimester of pregnancy,

166
00:10:45,885 --> 00:10:51,557
there are several facial processes that
need to fuse together.

167
00:10:51,932 --> 00:10:59,398
A cleft lip happens when the upper part of
the lip doesn’t fuse.

168
00:10:59,648 --> 00:11:07,448
While a cleft palate is an opening that
can extend up toward the roof of the mouth.

169
00:11:07,531 --> 00:11:11,660
Most of the time they occur together,
though sometimes they don’t.

170
00:11:11,952 --> 00:11:17,124
The causes are what
we call 'multifactorial'.

171
00:11:17,625 --> 00:11:19,460
Often, of course,

172
00:11:19,460 --> 00:11:21,921
there’s a genetic predisposition.

173
00:11:21,921 --> 00:11:26,800
Meaning there’s a
history of it in the family.

174
00:11:26,800 --> 00:11:30,095
Or it could be environmental factors.

175
00:11:30,262 --> 00:11:33,599
Like smoking, drinking alcohol,

176
00:11:33,599 --> 00:11:41,774
or certain medications
that affect normal tissue fusion.

