Boss, here!

265
00:15:42,014 --> 00:15:44,266
There! All set! Thank you!

266
00:15:44,349 --> 00:15:45,349
All good!

267
00:15:45,392 --> 00:15:47,394
What practice? What do you mean “practice”?

268
00:15:47,603 --> 00:15:49,438
We’ll pretend we’re Scarlet’s family.

269
00:15:49,605 --> 00:15:51,315
Got it? We’re doing role play.

270
00:15:51,607 --> 00:15:52,691
I’m the director.

271
00:15:53,901 --> 00:15:54,901
Mimi!

272
00:15:56,778 --> 00:15:58,280
You’ll be Scarlet, okay?

273
00:15:58,864 --> 00:16:00,115
Find something to wear.

274
00:16:00,199 --> 00:16:02,074
- Yes, sir!
- Collins!

275
00:16:03,535 --> 00:16:04,535
Come here.

276
00:16:06,788 --> 00:16:08,457
You’re the father, okay?

277
00:16:08,540 --> 00:16:10,584
Okay, sir. What should I wear?

278
00:16:11,168 --> 00:16:13,378
My God, Collins! Whatever you like!

279
00:16:13,420 --> 00:16:14,588
Do we even know them?

280
00:16:14,880 --> 00:16:17,966
Wear sportswear,
a national costume, anything!

281
00:16:18,133 --> 00:16:20,385
My God! You’re getting on my nerves!

282
00:16:20,636 --> 00:16:22,429
Okay, okay! Sorry, direk! Sorry!

283
00:16:22,679 --> 00:16:23,679
Me?

284
00:16:24,431 --> 00:16:26,600
I guess I’ll be the mom. I'll wear this.

285
00:16:29,686 --> 00:16:30,686
Direk?

286
00:16:30,896 --> 00:16:31,896
Direk?

287
00:16:32,064 --> 00:16:33,064
What about me?

288
00:16:33,315 --> 00:16:35,025
Am I included? What am I?

289
00:16:35,234 --> 00:16:37,486
Okay, Oxford.

290
00:16:38,362 --> 00:16:39,362
Wait.

291
00:16:41,114 --> 00:16:42,282
You’re their dog.

292
00:16:42,407 --> 00:16:43,407
Huh?

293
00:16:43,742 --> 00:16:46,078
A dog? Do I look like a dog?

294
00:16:46,537 --> 00:16:48,664
You all get good roles, and I’m the dog?

295
00:16:49,103 --> 00:16:51,243
- The hell...
- Oxford,

296
00:16:51,542 --> 00:16:54,503
in showbiz,
whether your role is big or small,

297
00:16:54,528 --> 00:16:56,168
what matters is you're part of the scene.

298
00:16:56,588 --> 00:16:57,588
Think about it:

299
00:16:57,673 --> 00:17:00,444
What if they really have a dog,
and we don’t get to practice that part?

300
00:17:00,468 --> 00:17:01,594
Then Ngo’s in trouble.

301
00:17:01,969 --> 00:17:03,333
Alright, let me hear your bark.

302
00:17:04,388 --> 00:17:05,388
Like this?

303
00:17:08,475 --> 00:17:11,144
Brilliant! See? Perfect!
Fits you perfectly!

304
00:17:14,314 --> 00:17:15,983
- Yeah, direk!
- Right?

305
00:17:16,275 --> 00:17:17,609
Thank you so much!

306
00:17:17,734 --> 00:17:19,402
- This works.
- Okay, go.

307
00:17:20,904 --> 00:17:21,904
Okay.

308
00:17:22,322 --> 00:17:24,616
This is the door. Okay?

309
00:17:24,741 --> 00:17:25,826
You’ll enter from there.

310
00:17:26,368 --> 00:17:27,703
Alright, we’re ready.

311
00:17:27,728 --> 00:17:29,605
Find your spots.

312
00:17:29,724 --> 00:17:30,806
In three, two, one,

313
00:17:30,831 --> 00:17:32,416
action! Go!

314
00:17:34,042 --> 00:17:35,836
Hello? Hello!

315
00:17:35,961 --> 00:17:36,961
Cut!

316
00:17:37,337 --> 00:17:38,422
What “hello”?

317
00:17:39,047 --> 00:17:40,924
What is this, the province? “Hello”?

318
00:17:41,967 --> 00:17:44,261
Are Scarlet’s family poor?
You saw they have a car, right?

319
00:17:44,845 --> 00:17:46,555
And you say “hello”? Use the doorbell!

320
00:17:47,901 --> 00:17:48,949
Take two.

321
00:17:48,974 --> 00:17:49,975
That was dumb.

322
00:17:50,893 --> 00:17:51,893
Okay, take two.

323
00:17:52,019 --> 00:17:53,395
In three, two, one,

324
00:17:53,645 --> 00:17:55,022
action! Doorbell!

325
00:17:55,606 --> 00:17:57,608
- Ding-dong!
- Good.

326
00:17:57,649 --> 00:17:59,026
- Ding-dong!
- Enter!

327
00:17:59,735 --> 00:18:00,735
Oh, Scarlet?

328
00:18:01,778 --> 00:18:02,778
Hello, Scarlet?

329
00:18:03,030 --> 00:18:04,314
Hi, Ngongo!

330
00:18:04,406 --> 00:18:06,240
- Hello!
- Cut!

331
00:18:07,492 --> 00:18:08,744
Mimi, what did you say?

332
00:18:09,453 --> 00:18:11,383
“Hi, Ngongo!” and “Hello!”

333
00:18:11,455 --> 00:18:13,298
Why? Does Scarlet have a harelip?

334
00:18:13,915 --> 00:18:15,584
No! Well, I cannot—

335
00:18:15,609 --> 00:18:16,609
Exactly!

336
00:18:16,752 --> 00:18:18,503
She speaks normally.
Can you do that?

337
00:18:18,833 --> 00:18:19,838
Uh, no.

338
00:18:19,863 --> 00:18:21,823
Then why did you speak?

339
00:18:22,257 --> 00:18:23,967
You’re ruining the character.

340
00:18:24,426 --> 00:18:25,927
It should feel real.

341
00:18:26,470 --> 00:18:27,638
Not like that.

342
00:18:28,221 --> 00:18:29,599
Say it like that again, I’ll punch you—

343
00:18:29,623 --> 00:18:31,750
- Okay, okay!
- Why did you even speak?

344
00:18:32,517 --> 00:18:33,852
- Easy! Easy!
- Oh my gosh!

345
00:18:33,977 --> 00:18:35,062
Why would she speak?

346
00:18:35,687 --> 00:18:36,938
Okay! Okay!

347
00:18:37,272 --> 00:18:39,733
Sorry, direk! Sorry, guys!

348
00:18:39,775 --> 00:18:41,568
Do it properly. Oh my God.

349
00:18:41,777 --> 00:18:42,777
You’re all so dumb.

350
00:18:43,236 --> 00:18:44,488
Alright, take three.

351
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:46,573
After the doorbell, enter.

352
00:18:46,598 --> 00:18:48,128
Scarlet, don’t talk.

353
00:18:48,784 --> 00:18:50,702
Copy? I’ll hit you with this chair.

354
00:18:51,161 --> 00:18:52,161
Don’t talk, okay?

355
00:18:52,836 --> 00:18:53,883
Okay.

356
00:18:53,908 --> 00:18:56,927
Take three in three, two, one…
action! Doorbell.

357
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,474
- Ding-dong!
- Enter.

358
00:18:58,710 --> 00:18:59,836
Scarlet, don’t talk.

359
00:19:01,088 --> 00:19:02,964
There. That's right. Go straight.

360
00:19:06,051 --> 00:19:07,302
Ow! Ow! Ow!

361
00:19:07,327 --> 00:19:08,804
- Cut!
- Ow!

362
00:19:08,845 --> 00:19:10,555
What was that? What happened?

363
00:19:10,722 --> 00:19:12,391
Oxford bit me!

364
00:19:12,933 --> 00:19:15,560
That hurt! Why’d you bite me?

365
00:19:16,228 --> 00:19:18,772
Oxford, why’d you bite him?
Why are you biting people?

366
00:19:18,980 --> 00:19:19,980
Hey!

367
00:19:20,649 --> 00:19:21,900
I’m a dog!

368
00:19:22,359 --> 00:19:23,359
Are you stupid?

369
00:19:23,568 --> 00:19:26,947
Of course I don’t know him.
He walked into the house.

370
00:19:27,197 --> 00:19:28,240
I’m gonna bite him.

371
00:19:28,865 --> 00:19:30,951
That's what dogs do. Right?

372
00:19:31,076 --> 00:19:32,869
Fair point? Okay.

373
00:19:33,161 --> 00:19:34,413
Okay, fine.

374
00:19:35,277 --> 00:19:36,348
Fair point.

375
00:19:36,373 --> 00:19:38,417
He should calm me down.

376
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,168
I’m a dog, after all.

377
00:19:40,193 --> 00:19:41,194
Okay, fine.

378
00:19:42,170 --> 00:19:43,170
Take four.

379
00:19:43,588 --> 00:19:46,258
Okay, in three, two, one, action!

380
00:19:46,925 --> 00:19:48,719
- Doorbell.
- Ding-dong!

381
00:19:48,802 --> 00:19:50,761
Enter. Scarlet!

382
00:19:51,346 --> 00:19:52,346
There!

383
00:19:52,489 --> 00:19:53,740
Okay, there’s the dog.

384
00:19:53,765 --> 00:19:54,766
Okay, okay. There!

385
00:19:54,766 --> 00:19:57,102
Good boy, good boy.

386
00:19:57,127 --> 00:19:59,129
Go to the father.
Ask for blessing.

387
00:20:00,272 --> 00:20:01,432
Sir, I ask for your blessing.

388
00:20:01,982 --> 00:20:03,400
Who are you?

389
00:20:03,567 --> 00:20:05,193
Cut! Cut! Cut!

390
00:20:05,318 --> 00:20:06,653
Why did you call cut?

391
00:20:06,653 --> 00:20:07,904
Only I call cut.

392
00:20:08,071 --> 00:20:10,157
Didn’t you see?
I was about to get shot.

393
00:20:10,157 --> 00:20:11,957
Why do you have a gun?
Where did you get that?

394
00:20:12,117 --> 00:20:15,287
That’s too much.
Is Scarlet’s family really that violent?

395
00:20:15,370 --> 00:20:16,788
That’s what Oxford said.

396
00:20:18,248 --> 00:20:19,248
Oh, um...

397
00:20:19,958 --> 00:20:21,732
Because he’s the father.

398
00:20:21,835 --> 00:20:24,045
That’s a natural reaction.
He’s the father.

399
00:20:24,171 --> 00:20:25,505
Look at me. I’m a dog, right?

400
00:20:25,714 --> 00:20:26,965
I’m super protective.

401
00:20:27,399 --> 00:20:29,109
That’s normal. He’s the father.

402
00:20:29,134 --> 00:20:30,469
He loves his children.

403
00:20:30,594 --> 00:20:32,429
Okay. Fine. Okay.

404
00:20:32,471 --> 00:20:34,973
But don’t point the gun.
That’s Ngo, come on.

405
00:20:34,973 --> 00:20:36,516
Why didn’t you ask for his blessing?

406
00:20:36,541 --> 00:20:38,251
Yeah, why didn’t you?

407
00:20:38,518 --> 00:20:41,605
Remember, respect! Respect!
We've been over this.

408
00:20:42,189 --> 00:20:43,189
Take five!

409
00:20:43,315 --> 00:20:44,315
Action!

410
00:20:44,340 --> 00:20:45,358
Doorbell.

411
00:20:45,358 --> 00:20:47,125
- Ding-dong!
- Enter.

412
00:20:47,152 --> 00:20:48,778
Scarlet. Don’t talk.

413
00:20:48,920 --> 00:20:50,672
There, calm the dog.

414
00:20:50,697 --> 00:20:52,073
Good boy. Good boy.

415
00:20:52,098 --> 00:20:53,475
Okay, bow to her father.

416
00:20:53,533 --> 00:20:54,693
Sir, I ask for your blessing.

417
00:20:55,327 --> 00:20:57,353
There. Now go to the mother.

418
00:20:58,038 --> 00:20:59,372
Ask for the mother's blessing.

419
00:20:59,664 --> 00:21:00,664
Uhm—

420
00:21:02,250 --> 00:21:03,293
Hello, mommy.

421
00:21:03,668 --> 00:21:04,668
Hello— Oh!

422
00:21:05,420 --> 00:21:06,420
What the fuck?

423
00:21:07,047 --> 00:21:08,298
Does he have a harelip?

424
00:21:08,465 --> 00:21:12,094
Hey! Cut! Cut!

425
00:21:12,302 --> 00:21:13,929
Don’t talk to Ngo like that!

426
00:21:14,029 --> 00:21:15,655
Yeah! He loves her!

427
00:21:15,680 --> 00:21:18,099
Why’d you insult him? That’s too much!

428
00:21:18,141 --> 00:21:19,184
Seriously!

429
00:21:19,226 --> 00:21:21,019
You know Ngo has a speech problem!

430
00:21:21,044 --> 00:21:24,256
Yeah. And is that how
Scarlet’s mom would act?

431
00:21:26,576 --> 00:21:28,318
Didn’t you hear what I said?

432
00:21:29,486 --> 00:21:31,446
Didn’t I say this is practice?

433
00:21:32,362 --> 00:21:34,865
Yeah, I know. He has a speech problem.

434
00:21:35,183 --> 00:21:37,769
But does Scarlet’s mom know that?

435
00:21:38,787 --> 00:21:40,080
Huh? Does she?

436
00:21:41,164 --> 00:21:42,164
She doesn’t, right?

437
00:21:43,208 --> 00:21:44,811
So what, she’s not allowed to be shocked?

438
00:21:44,835 --> 00:21:46,312
What, she just accepts it right away?

439
00:21:46,336 --> 00:21:48,255
This is the worst-case scenario.

440
00:21:49,047 --> 00:21:50,727
What happens if that's how they treat you?

441
00:21:51,007 --> 00:21:52,008
Is that how you’ll react?

442
00:21:52,926 --> 00:21:55,029
If they disrespect you,
will you disrespect them back?

443
00:21:55,053 --> 00:21:56,471
Right in front of Scarlet?

444
00:21:58,682 --> 00:21:59,766
Of course not.

445
00:22:00,725 --> 00:22:01,852
I’ll say,

446
00:22:02,143 --> 00:22:05,647
even if I have a harelip, my intentions
toward your daughter are good.

447
00:22:05,647 --> 00:22:07,566
There! That’s it!

448
00:22:07,691 --> 00:22:09,331
Stop acting like you know better than me!

449
00:22:09,901 --> 00:22:12,279
Then you be the director!

450
00:22:12,279 --> 00:22:13,947
My job’s so hard!

451
00:22:13,947 --> 00:22:15,073
- Easy! Easy! Easy!
- Calm down!

452
00:22:15,073 --> 00:22:16,283
You fucking idiots!

453
00:22:19,953 --> 00:22:21,621
Let’s just do this, please.

454
00:22:21,621 --> 00:22:22,706
Let’s finish this.

455
00:22:23,456 --> 00:22:24,499
Quick! From the top!

456
00:22:24,624 --> 00:22:26,209
Let’s go, let’s go!

457
00:22:27,878 --> 00:22:31,756
In three, two, one, action!

458
00:22:34,885 --> 00:22:36,636
Hi, Ngo. Come in.

459
00:22:42,392 --> 00:22:44,311
Bro, sit over there.

460
00:22:44,936 --> 00:22:46,187
Go to the other side.

461
00:22:47,355 --> 00:22:48,523
Hurry up!

462
00:22:49,441 --> 00:22:51,484
Ngo, come here. Come in.

463
00:22:52,235 --> 00:22:53,235
Sit here.

464
00:23:00,410 --> 00:23:01,410
Ngo,

465
00:23:01,745 --> 00:23:02,945
are you looking for something?

466
00:23:03,705 --> 00:23:05,582
Uh, no. Just looking around.

467
00:23:07,334 --> 00:23:08,585
Do you have a dog?

468
00:23:10,754 --> 00:23:12,797
Oh, you. You’re funny, Ngo.

469
00:23:12,964 --> 00:23:14,799
No. We don’t have a dog.

470
00:23:14,799 --> 00:23:15,799
Let,

471
00:23:15,884 --> 00:23:17,724
just have him sit so
you can leave right away.

472
00:23:18,219 --> 00:23:19,219
Bro, please.

473
00:23:20,513 --> 00:23:21,848
What I mean is,

474
00:23:22,307 --> 00:23:23,934
so you can both head out soon.

475
00:23:24,392 --> 00:23:26,645
Maybe you have somewhere to be.

476
00:23:26,853 --> 00:23:27,979
A meeting or something.

477
00:23:30,315 --> 00:23:31,900
Ngo, go ahead. Sit here.

478
00:23:32,609 --> 00:23:33,985
Thank you, ma’am.

479
00:23:36,196 --> 00:23:39,032
Sweetie, introduce us to your friend.

480
00:23:40,283 --> 00:23:41,826
What’s your name, hijo?

481
00:23:43,453 --> 00:23:44,496
I'm Ngongo, ma'am.

482
00:23:46,753 --> 00:23:47,766
Oh, hijo,

483
00:23:47,791 --> 00:23:50,085
what she means is what’s your real name?

484
00:23:50,210 --> 00:23:51,210
Your name?

485
00:23:52,462 --> 00:23:53,463
It’s really Ngo-Ngo.

486
00:23:57,884 --> 00:23:59,719
What Mom and Dad are asking

487
00:24:00,220 --> 00:24:01,460
is the name you were born with.

488
00:24:02,138 --> 00:24:03,682
The one on your birth certificate.

489
00:24:04,683 --> 00:24:06,142
Is that what your mother named you?

490
00:24:08,895 --> 00:24:09,896
Bro,

491
00:24:10,689 --> 00:24:11,689
Ma,

492
00:24:12,357 --> 00:24:13,357
Pa,

493
00:24:13,858 --> 00:24:16,403
his name really is “Ngongo.”

494
00:24:16,486 --> 00:24:17,946
And his nickname

495
00:24:18,196 --> 00:24:19,196
is Ngo.

496
00:24:20,532 --> 00:24:22,075
Oh, I see. Is that so?

497
00:24:22,450 --> 00:24:23,910
Sorry about that.

498
00:24:24,077 --> 00:24:26,079
We just couldn’t understand you.

499
00:24:26,955 --> 00:24:28,206
Alright, alright. Let’s eat.

500
00:24:28,373 --> 00:24:30,000
It’s bad to keep the food waiting.

501
00:24:30,250 --> 00:24:31,918
Dear, pass the coconut.

502
00:24:32,252 --> 00:24:33,628
And give some to Ngo too.

503
00:24:36,923 --> 00:24:37,923
Thank you.

504
00:24:45,849 --> 00:24:46,849
Are you okay?

505
00:24:46,975 --> 00:24:48,495
Why are you sipping through your nose?

506
00:24:48,768 --> 00:24:49,808
You should use your mouth.

507
00:24:50,145 --> 00:24:51,396
Maybe you should

508
00:24:51,813 --> 00:24:53,398
put the straw here

509
00:24:53,898 --> 00:24:55,150
so no air gets in.

510
00:24:55,483 --> 00:24:56,483
Boys.

511
00:24:57,402 --> 00:24:58,903
Bro, really.

512
00:25:00,196 --> 00:25:01,823
- Are you okay?
- I’m okay.

513
00:25:01,906 --> 00:25:04,743
Just eat. Please, go ahead and eat.

514
00:25:04,808 --> 00:25:05,837
- Rice?
- Yes.

515
00:25:05,923 --> 00:25:07,216
I’m okay. Later.

516
00:25:07,328 --> 00:25:08,580
I’ll just watch for now.

517
00:25:09,831 --> 00:25:10,831
Banana?

518
00:25:11,166 --> 00:25:12,417
I’ll just have a banana.

519
00:25:15,670 --> 00:25:17,547
Guys! Guys!

520
00:25:17,839 --> 00:25:19,507
It’s Ngo! He’s here!

521
00:25:21,593 --> 00:25:22,993
What happened? Did they have a dog?

522
00:25:23,386 --> 00:25:24,637
What’s up, lover boy?

523
00:25:24,971 --> 00:25:26,723
So how’d the meet-the-parents go?

524
00:25:27,015 --> 00:25:28,183
So, Ngo? Did they have a dog?

525
00:25:28,349 --> 00:25:30,226
What happened, Ngo? What happened?

526
00:25:31,603 --> 00:25:32,603
Ngo, what?

527
00:25:32,687 --> 00:25:33,687
Did they have a dog?

528
00:25:33,980 --> 00:25:35,440
What's with the suspense?

529
00:25:35,857 --> 00:25:39,027
- So?
- We failed. Totally failed.

530
00:25:40,737 --> 00:25:41,737
Ngo…

531
00:25:43,281 --> 00:25:44,281
What happened?

532
00:25:47,202 --> 00:25:49,245
Nothing, Ma. Let’s not talk about it.

533
00:25:51,164 --> 00:25:52,499
Come on, what?

534
00:25:53,166 --> 00:25:54,751
Did they have a dog?

535
00:25:55,376 --> 00:25:56,376
No!

536
00:25:57,587 --> 00:25:59,214
Her brother’s the one who hurt me.

537
00:26:00,006 --> 00:26:01,132
Damn it!

538
00:26:01,716 --> 00:26:02,926
So no dog after all.

539
00:26:03,718 --> 00:26:05,136
All that effort, wasted!

540
00:26:05,804 --> 00:26:07,555
I should’ve just been the brother, huh?

541
00:26:08,473 --> 00:26:09,974
Man, you guys are such clowns!

542
00:26:10,850 --> 00:26:13,186
- I’m out.
- Wait, where are you going?

543
00:26:13,211 --> 00:26:14,211
I'm walking out.

544
00:26:14,687 --> 00:26:16,147
Idiot.

545
00:26:18,458 --> 00:26:20,836
It's because you kept asking,
piece of shit! You’re so damn loud!

546
00:26:20,860 --> 00:26:22,320
I thought there was a dog!

547
00:26:22,345 --> 00:26:23,345
Hey!

548
00:26:23,655 --> 00:26:24,655
Shut up!

549
00:26:25,115 --> 00:26:26,741
I’ll punch you, okay?

550
00:26:26,908 --> 00:26:28,034
I’ll break your face.

551
00:26:29,099 --> 00:26:30,620
Stop talking, okay? Stop talking.

552
00:26:30,745 --> 00:26:32,038
Don’t say a word.

553
00:26:37,001 --> 00:26:38,795
Wow! So happy! Show-offs!

554
00:26:38,920 --> 00:26:40,255
You’re really going all out, huh!

555
00:26:43,633 --> 00:26:45,510
Straight-up eating each other’s faces.

556
00:26:45,510 --> 00:26:47,095
Your nose is all soaked!

557
00:26:47,470 --> 00:26:48,470
Sir!

558
00:26:48,638 --> 00:26:50,390
- Are these peanuts hot?
- Huh?

559
00:26:50,932 --> 00:26:51,932
Deaf.

560
00:26:52,517 --> 00:26:53,517
It’s so clear.

561
00:26:54,060 --> 00:26:55,239
You didn’t hear?

562
00:26:57,188 --> 00:26:58,731
Hey! Hey!

563
00:26:59,742 --> 00:27:00,775
Hey!

564
00:27:00,800 --> 00:27:03,040
These people are crazy. Right here,
on top of each other!

565
00:27:03,149 --> 00:27:04,149
Animals!

566
00:27:05,238 --> 00:27:06,409
Hey!

567
00:27:06,854 --> 00:27:08,578
- Why are you there?
- What’s your problem, man?

568
00:27:08,602 --> 00:27:09,617
