569
00:27:09,617 --> 00:27:11,720
You’re the ones on top of each other.
Like some softcore flick.

570
00:27:11,744 --> 00:27:13,888
- Pay for these, boss.
- Pay? Yeah, I’ll pay!

571
00:27:13,913 --> 00:27:15,915
What did they say?
Okay, never mind.

572
00:27:16,875 --> 00:27:17,959
Kids these days.

573
00:27:18,126 --> 00:27:20,206
So many people around
and you’re all over each other!

574
00:27:25,008 --> 00:27:26,968
I’ll just call Scarlet.

575
00:27:27,677 --> 00:27:29,053
Ma, seriously!

576
00:27:29,512 --> 00:27:30,890
You keep calling!

577
00:27:39,355 --> 00:27:40,355
Hello?

578
00:27:40,773 --> 00:27:41,773
Scarlet?

579
00:27:42,859 --> 00:27:43,860
Hello, Ngo?

580
00:27:44,152 --> 00:27:45,653
Why did you call?

581
00:27:46,654 --> 00:27:47,654
No, it’s just—

582
00:27:49,449 --> 00:27:51,618
I just wanted to ask—

583
00:27:51,618 --> 00:27:54,120
how you felt earlier.

584
00:27:54,120 --> 00:27:56,122
Were you turned off, or what?

585
00:27:56,122 --> 00:27:57,122
Huh?

586
00:27:57,498 --> 00:27:59,542
- What?
- Wait, um—

587
00:28:00,919 --> 00:28:01,961
I’m asking—

588
00:28:01,961 --> 00:28:03,087
how you felt earlier,

589
00:28:03,087 --> 00:28:04,631
were you turned off?

590
00:28:04,631 --> 00:28:06,007
What did you feel?

591
00:28:06,007 --> 00:28:07,007
Sorry, Ngo.

592
00:28:07,050 --> 00:28:09,010
I really can’t understand you, Choppy.

593
00:28:09,010 --> 00:28:10,094
Chop-choppy.

594
00:28:11,095 --> 00:28:12,095
There.

595
00:28:12,305 --> 00:28:13,848
Were you turned off earlier—

596
00:28:13,848 --> 00:28:16,726
earlier—were you turned off?

597
00:28:16,976 --> 00:28:18,770
Because earlier I
couldn’t tell what you felt.

598
00:28:18,770 --> 00:28:19,938
Were you turned off?

599
00:28:19,938 --> 00:28:21,481
Sorry, Ngo. It’s really choppy.

600
00:28:21,481 --> 00:28:22,481
Chop-choppy?

601
00:28:25,318 --> 00:28:27,320
How about now? Hello?

602
00:28:27,820 --> 00:28:29,572
Can you hear me? Were you turned off?

603
00:28:29,572 --> 00:28:30,823
Were you turned off earlier?

604
00:28:30,823 --> 00:28:32,033
How did you feel?

605
00:28:32,116 --> 00:28:33,451
Huh? What was that?

606
00:28:33,868 --> 00:28:35,745
Were you turned off? Turned off!

607
00:28:36,454 --> 00:28:37,580
It’s choppy, Ngo.

608
00:28:37,914 --> 00:28:39,582
Turn— I’ll just turn this off!

609
00:28:40,708 --> 00:28:42,001
You keep saying it’s choppy,

610
00:28:42,001 --> 00:28:43,544
my mouth’s the one that’s chopped up!

611
00:28:45,129 --> 00:28:46,129
Damn it.

612
00:29:56,951 --> 00:29:59,620
Ngo, I’m sorry, okay?

613
00:29:59,912 --> 00:30:02,040
I really couldn’t understand you.

614
00:30:02,290 --> 00:30:04,042
Maybe it was the signal?

615
00:30:05,251 --> 00:30:07,128
Ah, no— it was the phone.

616
00:30:07,337 --> 00:30:09,088
I already threw it away. It sucked.

617
00:30:10,798 --> 00:30:11,841
That explains it.

618
00:30:11,841 --> 00:30:14,510
I tried calling you again the next day,

619
00:30:14,510 --> 00:30:16,095
but you weren’t reachable anymore.

620
00:30:16,929 --> 00:30:20,309
So I didn't try again.
Anyway, like I said,

621
00:30:21,642 --> 00:30:23,642
