for those flowers you just trashed.

1064
00:58:25,450 --> 00:58:28,336
They stayed up all
night researching for this.

1065
00:58:28,578 --> 00:58:30,471
From the flowers

1066
00:58:30,569 --> 00:58:32,988
to Scarlet’s favorite candle scent.

1067
00:58:34,417 --> 00:58:35,417
Oxford—

1068
00:58:36,836 --> 00:58:38,421
he fixed everything here.

1069
00:58:39,448 --> 00:58:41,533
He cooked, bought drinks—

1070
00:58:43,034 --> 00:58:44,369
even borrowed money

1071
00:58:44,969 --> 00:58:51,017
for this dinner you just ruined
because you keep putting yourself down!

1072
00:58:53,074 --> 00:58:54,241
Wow. Wow. Wow.

1073
00:58:55,271 --> 00:58:56,631
So now you’re throwing that at me?

1074
00:58:58,191 --> 00:58:59,734
You keeping score?

1075
00:59:00,443 --> 00:59:03,154
Then what about all
the times I helped you?

1076
00:59:04,500 --> 00:59:06,752
Who helped you graduate?
Wasn’t that me?

1077
00:59:07,503 --> 00:59:09,088
Wow. Wow. Wow.

1078
00:59:09,719 --> 00:59:13,639
Then what about the blood I donated
when you had dengue?

1079
00:59:13,664 --> 00:59:16,102
Then I shouldn’t have taken your blood!

1080
00:59:16,441 --> 00:59:18,610
Should’ve just let the
bad luck stay with you!

1081
00:59:18,971 --> 00:59:19,971
Wow! Wow!

1082
00:59:20,542 --> 00:59:23,086
Now it’s “bad luck”?

1083
00:59:23,966 --> 00:59:26,523
During the pandemic,
who helped you?

1084
00:59:27,220 --> 00:59:29,340
Remember when your mom's burger
stand got closed down?

1085
00:59:30,223 --> 00:59:31,223
Who helped you?

1086
00:59:32,266 --> 00:59:33,266
Us!

1087
00:59:33,351 --> 00:59:34,519
Ngo, it was us!

1088
00:59:34,747 --> 00:59:38,417
Oh, so you helped me. So what?
Didn’t I pay you back?

1089
00:59:38,523 --> 00:59:40,003
Now you’re gonna throw it in my face?

1090
00:59:40,066 --> 00:59:41,066
That’s enough!

1091
00:59:43,486 --> 00:59:45,442
Oxford, don’t waste your time.

1092
00:59:46,739 --> 00:59:48,449
You’re being unfair.

1093
00:59:48,474 --> 00:59:49,559
Oh, why?

1094
00:59:54,455 --> 00:59:55,748
Every time you fall for someone,

1095
00:59:56,541 --> 00:59:58,209
you only think about yourself.

1096
01:00:00,586 --> 01:00:03,106
You can love someone without forgetting
the people who love you.

1097
01:00:04,173 --> 01:00:09,220
Without hurting the people
who want that for you.

1098
01:00:11,472 --> 01:00:12,765
You know what your problem is?

1099
01:00:13,416 --> 01:00:14,834
Huh?

1100
01:00:16,477 --> 01:00:18,187
You’re too hard on yourself.

1101
01:00:18,479 --> 01:00:19,772
Yeah, I am!

1102
01:00:22,692 --> 01:00:24,652
I am! I’m the worst!

1103
01:00:27,113 --> 01:00:28,865
I tear myself down,

1104
01:00:30,908 --> 01:00:33,452
so when people do it,
it doesn’t hurt anymore!

1105
01:00:33,477 --> 01:00:34,992
It doesn’t hurt!

1106
01:00:39,724 --> 01:00:41,961
I don’t even know
why I went after Scarlet.

1107
01:00:43,271 --> 01:00:44,981
I already know what people will say.

1108
01:00:45,006 --> 01:00:48,009
Look at this guy.
He's got a lot of nerve.

1109
01:00:48,926 --> 01:00:50,212
Trying to court someone?

1110
01:00:51,512 --> 01:00:53,389
Like he doesn't have a harelip.

1111
01:00:57,727 --> 01:00:59,812
It was Scarlet's brothers
who did this to me.

1112
01:01:02,398 --> 01:01:03,816
I should’ve fought for it.

1113
01:01:04,730 --> 01:01:05,898
But how?

1114
01:01:06,903 --> 01:01:09,113
Isn’t this how it is for people like me?

1115
01:01:11,490 --> 01:01:14,702
You want to be accepted,
you let people mock you.

1116
01:01:16,353 --> 01:01:18,438
You have to let
people make fun of you.

1117
01:01:20,666 --> 01:01:22,710
You just take it.

1118
01:01:27,169 --> 01:01:28,462
That’s what I’ve been doing.

1119
01:01:29,634 --> 01:01:31,969
I kept on enduring it.
I just endure it.

1120
01:01:34,180 --> 01:01:35,473
So that I can be accepted.

1121
01:01:37,767 --> 01:01:40,280
Because I really like Scarlet.

1122
01:01:42,772 --> 01:01:44,440
I fall in love like everyone else.

1123
01:01:46,567 --> 01:01:48,319
I can love like everyone else.

1124
01:01:49,779 --> 01:01:52,214
Even if I know no one’s going
to love me back.

1125
01:01:53,157 --> 01:01:54,604
Because I was born into this!

1126
01:01:55,868 --> 01:01:56,868
Right?

1127
01:01:57,328 --> 01:01:58,441
This is who we are.

1128
01:01:59,664 --> 01:02:00,664
Right?

1129
01:02:01,791 --> 01:02:03,968
No one’s ever gonna understand us!

1130
01:02:05,697 --> 01:02:09,575
Yeah, I'm harsh towards myself.
I really am!

1131
01:02:12,260 --> 01:02:14,303
I even thought about ending it.

1132
01:02:15,805 --> 01:02:20,217
But what’s the point? I already feel like
I’m gasping for air.

1133
01:02:22,436 --> 01:02:24,230
I wanted to cut everything off—

1134
01:02:26,023 --> 01:02:27,191
But what for?

1135
01:02:28,109 --> 01:02:29,425
I’m already torn up,

1136
01:02:30,569 --> 01:02:31,712
I’m already torn open.

1137
01:02:31,737 --> 01:02:33,531
Wide open. So wide!

1138
01:02:36,492 --> 01:02:38,054
I just want to destroy everything!

1139
01:02:39,412 --> 01:02:41,080
I want to lose it!

1140
01:02:43,124 --> 01:02:45,251
I want to lose it!

1141
01:02:49,005 --> 01:02:50,131
Because I know

1142
01:02:51,757 --> 01:02:54,093
no one’s ever gonna love me.

1143
01:02:55,261 --> 01:02:58,681
No one’s ever gonna love us!

1144
01:03:01,934 --> 01:03:03,102
That’s not true.

1145
01:03:04,645 --> 01:03:06,188
That’s too much.

1146
01:03:08,733 --> 01:03:09,957
Scarlet.

1147
01:03:11,152 --> 01:03:12,445
I’m sorry.

1148
01:03:30,129 --> 01:03:31,129
Scarlet…

1149
01:03:33,732 --> 01:03:36,754
- Sorry. I can’t… I can’t—
- It's okay.

1150
01:03:38,070 --> 01:03:39,331
It’s okay.

1151
01:03:39,472 --> 01:03:40,472
I understand.

1152
01:03:42,808 --> 01:03:44,092
You know what...

1153
01:03:45,686 --> 01:03:47,396
maybe we should stop this.

1154
01:03:50,399 --> 01:03:53,235
If you want to file
a case against my brothers,

1155
01:03:54,570 --> 01:03:55,943
I’ll testify.

1156
01:03:56,364 --> 01:03:58,274
You deserve justice.

1157
01:04:03,398 --> 01:04:04,982
But I’m sorry.

1158
01:04:07,166 --> 01:04:09,794
I can’t let you court me anymore.

1159
01:04:13,434 --> 01:04:16,270
Because how can I believe

1160
01:04:16,874 --> 01:04:18,167
that you love me

1161
01:04:20,513 --> 01:04:22,163
when you can’t even

1162
01:04:23,349 --> 01:04:24,975
love yourself?

1163
01:04:37,405 --> 01:04:39,698
Your mom’s waiting for you.

1164
01:04:44,537 --> 01:04:45,996
I’m sorry, Ngo.

1165
01:05:22,616 --> 01:05:24,924
I can’t really blame you, dear.

1166
01:05:28,372 --> 01:05:30,583
I know it’s heavy,

1167
01:05:32,585 --> 01:05:33,585
it’s hard,

1168
01:05:35,421 --> 01:05:36,547
it really hurts.

1169
01:05:39,467 --> 01:05:42,136
People like you now—

1170
01:05:43,721 --> 01:05:45,681
in two, three hours,

1171
01:05:46,182 --> 01:05:48,225
their problem’s solved
with a simple surgery.

1172
01:05:49,393 --> 01:05:50,686
But back then, for you,

1173
01:05:53,355 --> 01:05:55,149
the operation was hard—

1174
01:05:59,403 --> 01:06:01,864
and the cost was even heavier.

1175
01:06:07,995 --> 01:06:10,247
So it hurts me too

1176
01:06:12,124 --> 01:06:14,168
when I see you like this.

1177
01:06:19,965 --> 01:06:20,965
So,

1178
01:06:24,303 --> 01:06:26,130
you can be angry at me.

1179
01:06:28,015 --> 01:06:31,322
Forgive me, son.
Be mad if you want.

1180
01:06:36,023 --> 01:06:37,691
I’m not blaming you, Ma.

1181
01:06:39,276 --> 01:06:40,276
Not even a little.

1182
01:06:42,780 --> 01:06:44,482
I’m angry at the world.

1183
01:06:47,451 --> 01:06:49,119
But I’m not angry at you.

1184
01:06:51,789 --> 01:06:54,291
But why are you angry at the world?

1185
01:06:58,087 --> 01:07:02,091
Yes, you have condition
but that wasn't your choice.

1186
01:07:03,384 --> 01:07:07,179
Now, if people choose

1187
01:07:08,138 --> 01:07:11,100
to mock and step on others,

1188
01:07:11,809 --> 01:07:13,811
I'd call that a condition as well.

1189
01:07:17,439 --> 01:07:18,686
Maybe that’s it, Ma.

1190
01:07:20,776 --> 01:07:22,611
This crack on my face,

1191
01:07:26,198 --> 01:07:29,285
it’s not just on my lips anymore.

1192
01:07:30,869 --> 01:07:32,788
It’s in who I am.

1193
01:07:36,709 --> 01:07:38,377
Ever since I was a child,

1194
01:07:39,420 --> 01:07:41,922
the world’s been trying to break me.

1195
01:07:44,550 --> 01:07:46,802
Ma, do you know?

1196
01:07:47,886 --> 01:07:49,722
I feel completely broken.

1197
01:07:50,973 --> 01:07:52,600
Completely broken, Ma.

1198
01:07:52,600 --> 01:07:55,444
That’s how the world sees me.

1199
01:07:56,061 --> 01:07:57,479
Broken.

1200
01:07:57,688 --> 01:07:59,857
That’s not true.

1201
01:07:59,857 --> 01:08:02,401
That’s not true, dear.

1202
01:08:03,482 --> 01:08:05,859
It is, Ma. It’s true.

1203
01:08:07,489 --> 01:08:08,489
Dear,

1204
01:08:09,450 --> 01:08:13,370
the world isn’t just
one or a few people,

1205
01:08:13,912 --> 01:08:15,706
so don’t generalize.

1206
01:08:17,207 --> 01:08:21,170
Ma, all of them look down on me.

1207
01:08:22,504 --> 01:08:24,327
Don’t say that.

1208
01:08:24,715 --> 01:08:27,134
It’s true, Ma. It’s true.

1209
01:08:35,601 --> 01:08:39,021
You think they look down on you

1210
01:08:40,022 --> 01:08:42,274
because that’s what you want
to believe about them.

1211
01:08:45,402 --> 01:08:47,613
Not everyone will judge you.

1212
01:08:49,490 --> 01:08:53,702
At first, they might laugh.

1213
01:08:54,536 --> 01:08:56,538
But once they get to know you,

1214
01:08:57,748 --> 01:08:59,541
that’s when they’ll see,

1215
01:09:00,125 --> 01:09:02,169
that’s when they’ll know

1216
01:09:03,337 --> 01:09:05,631
how good you really are.

1217
01:09:08,425 --> 01:09:11,804
Happy birthday to you.

1218
01:09:12,638 --> 01:09:16,308
- Happy birthday, happy birthday.
- There’s Ngo.

1219
01:09:16,565 --> 01:09:18,243
- Happy birthday—
- Ngo.

1220
01:09:18,268 --> 01:09:20,104
Starting your concert early, huh?

1221
01:09:22,147 --> 01:09:24,024
Happy birthday—

1222
01:09:24,149 --> 01:09:26,616
Queen’s so lucky, huh?

1223
01:09:27,044 --> 01:09:29,963
I hope we have a child
like Ngo someday.

1224
01:09:29,988 --> 01:09:30,989
Thoughtful.

1225
01:09:30,989 --> 01:09:31,990
I hope so.

1226
01:09:31,990 --> 01:09:33,437
And hardworking!

1227
01:09:33,951 --> 01:09:36,954
Sometimes, you think

1228
01:09:36,954 --> 01:09:39,710
you wished for something
but it wasn't given to you—

1229
01:09:40,833 --> 01:09:42,574
you think you’re being looked down on—

1230
01:09:44,253 --> 01:09:45,546
but the truth is,

1231
01:09:45,879 --> 01:09:48,257
they actually think highly of you.

1232
01:09:48,674 --> 01:09:50,634
Higher than you think.

1233
01:09:51,177 --> 01:09:52,256
Oh?

1234
01:09:52,386 --> 01:09:55,681
Where’s Ngo? He’s the one
who’ll light the torch.

1235
01:09:56,223 --> 01:09:59,143
You think no one believes in you,

1236
01:10:00,060 --> 01:10:04,064
that no one trusts you
because of your speech—

1237
01:10:04,064 --> 01:10:05,899
Forward, brothers!

1238
01:10:09,653 --> 01:10:14,366
But the truth is,
they trust you deeply

1239
01:10:14,717 --> 01:10:17,720
because they know
they can rely on you,

1240
01:10:17,745 --> 01:10:19,455
so they follow you.

1241
01:10:20,797 --> 01:10:23,508
Forward!

1242
01:10:25,394 --> 01:10:27,229
You think

1243
01:10:27,254 --> 01:10:31,008
their laughter and noise

1244
01:10:31,033 --> 01:10:34,190
mean they want you to fail—

1245
01:10:34,636 --> 01:10:37,848
but really, they’re shouting

1246
01:10:37,873 --> 01:10:41,370
because they’re cheering you on.

1247
01:10:42,369 --> 01:10:44,621
They’re the ones you don’t understand.

1248
01:10:44,646 --> 01:10:46,528
Hey!

1249
01:10:46,565 --> 01:10:47,608
Why'd he leave?

1250
01:10:47,733 --> 01:10:50,778
Ma’am, we’re just cheering for him.

1251
01:10:50,961 --> 01:10:52,504
Yes, ma’am.

1252
01:10:52,529 --> 01:10:54,782
We wanted him to win.

1253
01:10:54,807 --> 01:10:57,017
He was so close to winning.

1254
01:10:57,159 --> 01:10:59,077
- Yes, ma’am.
- Yes, ma’am.

1255
01:10:59,846 --> 01:11:03,141
Sometimes, you’re not being insulted,

1256
01:11:04,208 --> 01:11:06,126
you’re not being rejected,

1257
01:11:07,866 --> 01:11:12,129
but you’ve already judged it that way

1258
01:11:13,275 --> 01:11:15,027
because you don’t accept yourself.

1259
01:11:15,052 --> 01:11:18,889
When really, people
just have other reasons.

1260
01:11:19,156 --> 01:11:20,824
Hey, why don’t you want to?

1261
01:11:20,849 --> 01:11:24,686
I got my period and
I'm worried Ngo might see!

1262
01:11:24,894 --> 01:11:25,896
You're right.

1263
01:11:25,921 --> 01:11:27,005
So that's why.

1264
01:11:27,731 --> 01:11:29,566
That’s why I was shy in front of Ngo.

1265
01:11:30,884 --> 01:11:33,594
And because you don’t accept yourself,

1266
01:11:35,656 --> 01:11:40,118
you deny yourself happiness and success.

1267
01:11:41,345 --> 01:11:43,055
128. It is correct!

1268
01:11:43,080 --> 01:11:44,420
We have our winner!

1269
01:11:52,798 --> 01:11:54,174
Congratulations!

1270
01:11:54,174 --> 01:11:55,384
Thank you, sir.

1271
01:11:58,178 --> 01:11:59,346
Too bad.

1272
01:12:00,389 --> 01:12:03,642
You think everything they’ll say

1273
01:12:03,976 --> 01:12:06,411
will hurt you.

1274
01:12:06,436 --> 01:12:10,816
You think all they
can give you is ridicule.

1275
01:12:11,900 --> 01:12:12,985
But the truth is,

1276
01:12:14,319 --> 01:12:18,532
you’re the one not giving
them the chance

1277
01:12:18,991 --> 01:12:21,201
to be kind to you.

1278
01:12:21,451 --> 01:12:22,744
What’s this?

1279
01:12:23,954 --> 01:12:26,164
It’s Ngo’s birthday tomorrow.
Let’s chip in two pesos each.

1280
01:12:26,164 --> 01:12:29,116
We’re just excited because
it’s his birthday tomorrow.

1281
01:12:30,976 --> 01:12:35,003
And when you take that
chance away from them,

1282
01:12:35,128 --> 01:12:38,694
let us offer each other a sign of peace.

1283
01:12:39,761 --> 01:12:41,555
You’re the one who suffers.

1284
01:12:43,223 --> 01:12:45,809
You’re the one who loses your peace.

1285
01:12:56,445 --> 01:12:57,445
My dear,

1286
01:13:00,616 --> 01:13:02,880
I love you so much.

1287
01:13:03,827 --> 01:13:05,397
Remember that.

1288
01:13:07,664 --> 01:13:09,124
And I don’t want you

1289
01:13:09,809 --> 01:13:12,436
living your life in sadness.

1290
01:13:14,796 --> 01:13:16,052
I don’t want

1291
01:13:17,424 --> 01:13:21,887
your heart to be full of anger.

1292
01:13:25,223 --> 01:13:27,495
Do you know why?

1293
01:13:30,960 --> 01:13:32,253
Because to me,

1294
01:13:33,672 --> 01:13:35,174
there’s nothing wrong with you.

1295
01:13:42,407 --> 01:13:43,700
Do you know,

1296
01:13:44,576 --> 01:13:46,456
from the day you were born

1297
01:13:47,955 --> 01:13:50,248
until you learned to speak,

1298
01:13:52,250 --> 01:13:54,920
the first word you ever said

1299
01:13:56,505 --> 01:13:59,141
is a word that, even now,

1300
01:14:00,217 --> 01:14:04,972
when you say it, sounds
completely smooth.

1301
01:14:06,223 --> 01:14:08,642
It’s clear,

1302
01:14:11,061 --> 01:14:12,646
beautiful to hear,

1303
01:14:14,064 --> 01:14:15,649
and I feel it deeply.

1304
01:14:17,401 --> 01:14:19,027
Do you know what it is?

1305
01:14:27,077 --> 01:14:28,745
What do you call me?

1306
01:14:30,789 --> 01:14:37,254
Mama!

1307
01:14:40,007 --> 01:14:45,512
Mama!

1308
01:15:15,667 --> 01:15:19,371
Grant us peace and unity.

1309
01:15:19,555 --> 01:15:22,016
According to your will.

1310
01:15:22,090 --> 01:15:26,676
Together with the Holy Spirit,
forever and ever.

1311
01:15:27,779 --> 01:15:30,741
Peace be with you always.

1312
01:15:30,766 --> 01:15:32,225
And also with you.

1313
01:15:32,250 --> 01:15:35,754
Let us offer each other a sign of peace.

1314
01:15:35,896 --> 01:15:46,394
- Peace be with you.
- Peace be with you.

1315
01:15:46,573 --> 01:15:47,657
Ngo’s here.

1316
01:15:47,716 --> 01:15:49,426
Roll your eyes at him.
All together, okay?

1317
01:15:49,451 --> 01:15:51,161
Okay. One, two, three, go.

1318
01:16:09,262 --> 01:16:11,473
Hey! Hey! Please stop ignoring me!

1319
01:16:12,320 --> 01:16:13,325
Hey!

1320
01:16:13,350 --> 01:16:16,489
Even God forgives—
what’s wrong with you guys!

1321
01:16:18,188 --> 01:16:19,898
Wait! I have something to say.

1322
01:16:20,107 --> 01:16:21,316
Then say it!

1323
01:16:22,400 --> 01:16:23,400
Then say it!

1324
01:16:23,944 --> 01:16:25,695
You say whatever
you want anyway, right?

1325
01:16:38,500 --> 01:16:40,252
Lord, help me.

1326
01:16:49,453 --> 01:16:50,662
“I love you.”

1327
01:16:52,639 --> 01:16:53,932
Why’d you press it?

1328
01:16:54,724 --> 01:16:55,851
Why’d you press it?

1329
01:16:57,185 --> 01:16:58,728
What if I press your mouth?

1330
01:16:59,646 --> 01:17:02,274
Before you do anything,
say sorry first.

1331
01:17:03,108 --> 01:17:05,848
Wait, here it is.

1332
01:17:07,752 --> 01:17:09,087
What are you sorry for?

1333
01:17:10,924 --> 01:17:12,968
For all the wrong things
I’ve done to you.

1334
01:17:12,993 --> 01:17:13,993
Like what?

1335
01:17:15,787 --> 01:17:18,165
Like the hurtful words I said.

1336
01:17:19,416 --> 01:17:20,416
That’s it?

1337
01:17:22,544 --> 01:17:23,628
And for...

1338
01:17:25,005 --> 01:17:27,760
hurting you physically.

1339
01:17:29,196 --> 01:17:30,280
That all you’ve got?

1340
01:17:30,886 --> 01:17:32,596
If that’s it, we’re leaving. Come on.

1341
01:17:32,621 --> 01:17:33,914
No, no, wait.

1342
01:17:36,433 --> 01:17:37,517
And more than anything,

1343
01:17:38,685 --> 01:17:41,362
I didn’t see your love for me.

1344
01:17:43,148 --> 01:17:44,825
I kept thinking that…

1345
01:17:45,942 --> 01:17:47,444
others understood me.

1346
01:17:50,614 --> 01:17:53,387
But I forgot that you were
the ones who were there for me

1347
01:17:53,742 --> 01:17:55,410
more times than I can count.

1348
01:17:57,412 --> 01:17:58,997
I forgot that

1349
01:18:00,790 --> 01:18:02,959
you’re the ones who
really understand me.

1350
01:18:04,375 --> 01:18:08,379
Even if sometimes it’s hard
for us to understand each other…

1351
01:18:10,008 --> 01:18:13,887
you know what’s in my heart.

1352
01:18:15,263 --> 01:18:16,263
So…

1353
01:18:17,432 --> 01:18:19,142
Guys, sorry.

1354
01:18:20,310 --> 01:18:21,445
I’m really sorry.

1355
01:18:24,064 --> 01:18:25,523
Ngo, come here.

1356
01:18:27,992 --> 01:18:28,992
Damn it.

1357
01:18:30,483 --> 01:18:31,483
Damn you!

1358
01:18:32,906 --> 01:18:34,241
Don’t ever do that again, okay?

1359
01:18:35,200 --> 01:18:36,200
Do what?

1360
01:18:36,225 --> 01:18:37,709
Get yourself beaten up.

1361
01:18:38,745 --> 01:18:40,664
You might get another cut on your lip.

1362
01:18:41,165 --> 01:18:42,374
Criss-cross this time.

1363
01:18:42,399 --> 01:18:44,982
Knock on wood!

1364
01:18:45,007 --> 01:18:46,050
Let’s go! Let’s go!

1365
01:18:46,075 --> 01:18:47,869
Come on, let’s go!

1366
01:18:48,421 --> 01:18:52,300
You know, I still have some savings left.

1367
01:18:52,300 --> 01:18:54,135
What if we go to Boracay?

1368
01:18:54,160 --> 01:18:56,798
Wow! Are you gonna move on in Bora?

1369
01:18:56,972 --> 01:18:57,972
Yeah!

1370
01:18:58,515 --> 01:19:02,244
A Boracay trip to get
her out of my head!

1371
01:19:02,269 --> 01:19:04,162
Wow!

1372
01:19:04,187 --> 01:19:06,112
Word play.

1373
01:19:07,357 --> 01:19:09,192
Let’s go!
And get dreadlocks too.

1374
01:19:09,217 --> 01:19:11,803
So you’ll have more pull with the girls.

1375
01:19:11,889 --> 01:19:14,251
What if Scarlet comes to visit you?

1376
01:19:14,864 --> 01:19:15,864
No way!

1377
01:19:15,972 --> 01:19:17,938
Over my dead body.

1378
01:19:17,963 --> 01:19:20,418
No way!
It’s her loss, not mine.

1379
01:19:20,443 --> 01:19:21,528
Then let’s do this—

1380
01:19:21,553 --> 01:19:22,971
let’s get back at her brothers

1381
01:19:22,996 --> 01:19:24,081
and I’ll beat them up right now—

1382
01:19:24,105 --> 01:19:25,625
Hey! Stop! Stop!

1383
01:19:25,650 --> 01:19:27,247
You just came from church!

1384
01:19:27,585 --> 01:19:28,585
Right, yeah.

1385
01:19:29,045 --> 01:19:30,325
I'll beat them up tomorrow then.

1386
01:19:33,591 --> 01:19:34,917
Can I help you?

1387
01:19:35,051 --> 01:19:36,428
Damn it, I’m so pissed!

1388
01:19:37,012 --> 01:19:39,264
I'll give them both a harelip!

1389
01:19:40,660 --> 01:19:43,184
I'll shuffle their asses like cards.

1390
01:19:43,231 --> 01:19:45,025
Hey! Wasn’t I the dog?

1391
01:19:45,050 --> 01:19:47,706
- Yeah.
- I'll bite them to pieces!
